    "body": "## Overview\n\nPreserve all Kimi-Audio embeddings when multiple requests are batched. The current implementation takes only the first item's embeddings and silently leaves later audio placeholders unfused.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Batched embedding fusion agrees with processing each request separately, including unequal audio lengths and chunked prefill windows.\n- Text-only positions, output dtype, and the existing (text + audio) * sqrt(2) formula are preserved.\n\n## Validation\n\nDraft: not ready for merge. Full-model generation evaluation and human line-by-line review remain outstanding; no end-to-end serving result is claimed.\n\nOn macOS arm64, Python 3.12.13 and PyTorch 2.14.1, using the actual imported model method with a small text embedding layer:\n\n```sh\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/models/multimodal/processing/test_kimi_audio_embed.py -q\n```\n\nBefore: 6 failed, 2 passed. After: 8 passed. Tests cover list/tuple/batched tensor forms, fp32/bf16, two distinguishable audio items, interleaved text, scheduled windows, and text-only inputs.\n\n`pre-commit run --files vllm/model_executor/models/kimi_audio.py tests/models/multimodal/processing/test_kimi_audio_embed.py` passed. The standard precompiled installation could not find a cu130 arm64 wheel; Python-level tests ran against the checkout with common dependencies installed. These unit tests do not establish full-model accuracy or GPU serving correctness.\n\n## Details\n\nThe engine gathers per-item embeddings in scheduled request order, while the model previously selected `multimodal_embeddings[0]` and truncated the positions to that item's length. Reuse the existing multimodal merge helper for the entire collection, save text at the mask, and apply the existing fusion formula. No encoder, scheduler, or shared helper changes.\n\nDuplicate-work searches of open upstream PRs for `Kimi audio embedding`, `\"Kimi-Audio\"`, and `\"kimi_audio.py\"` did not identify the same embedding fusion fix. No upstream issue number is associated with this change. AI assistance (OpenAI Codex) was used to investigate, implement, and test this draft. Human review and model evaluation are explicitly pending.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
